Description: Stop gala aborting on exit with hot-corner barriers still active.
 .
 On exit mutter frees the X11 backend and asserts that no pointer barriers
 remain (meta_x11_barriers_free). Mutter never releases the gala plugin, so
 the hot corners keep their barriers and gala aborts, which makes the gala
 unit fail and ends the session. Remove the hot corners when the display
 emits "closing", as gnome-shell does on shutdown; this reuses the path
 monitor changes already take.
--- gala-8.6.1+r3147+pkg134~ubuntu8.1+ep1.orig/src/HotCorners/HotCornerManager.vala
+++ gala-8.6.1+r3147+pkg134~ubuntu8.1+ep1/src/HotCorners/HotCornerManager.vala
@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@
         behavior_settings.changed.connect (configure);
         unowned var monitor_manager = wm.get_display ().get_context ().get_backend ().get_monitor_manager ();
         monitor_manager.monitors_changed.connect (configure);
+        // mutter asserts every X11 barrier is gone when it frees the backend on exit
+        wm.get_display ().closing.connect (remove_all_hot_corners);
     }
 
     public void configure () {
